// Fuzz target: jwx_jwe. A JWE, compact or JSON, parsed; each recipient's
// merged header read and, where a fixed key fits its alg, its CEK unwrapped
// and the content decrypted (dir, A128KW, A256GCMKW, RSA1_5, RSA-OAEP,
// ECDH-ES(+KW) on P-256, P-384 and X25519 keys from RFC 7520's cookbook);
// then decrypt and decrypt_set.
//
// PBES2 is never tried: no key here is a password and PBES2 algs are
// skipped, since p2c comes from the input (known: jwe has no recipient cap
// and N x PBES2 is slow, review finding jwx/jwe.goose:1025-1064). For the
// same reason only the first MAX_RECIPIENTS recipients are tried, and
// decrypt/decrypt_set (which walk them all) are called only when there are
// no more than that.

import std;
import gslib from "../..";
import gslib.jwx;
import gslib.jwx.jwa;
import gslib.jwx.jwk;
import gslib.jwx.jwe;

